* --------------------------------------------------- operational amplifiers
* A macro model: input resistance, a transconductance stage (open-loop gain AOL, the gain-
* bandwidth GBW from its dominant pole, the slew rate from its limited current), the output
* clamped VHI below the positive and VLO above the negative supply (never past the middle of them:
* supplies that are not up yet do not short the clamps), ROUT behind it, RQ between the supplies.
.subckt OPAMP_MACRO inp inn vcc vee out params: gbw=1Meg aol=100k vhi=0.1 vlo=0.1 slew=1Meg rout=50 rq=20k
Rin inp inn 10Meg
Cinp inp 0 2p
Cinn inn 0 2p
Bmid mid 0 V = (V(vcc)+V(vee))/2
Bgm mid n1 I = max(min({aol}*1u*V(inp,inn), {slew*aol/(6.2831853*gbw*1Meg)}), -{slew*aol/(6.2831853*gbw*1Meg)})
Rn1 n1 mid 1Meg
Cn1 n1 mid {aol/(6.2831853*gbw*1Meg)}
Bhi hi 0 V = max(V(vcc)-{vhi}, V(mid)+1m)
Blo lo 0 V = min(V(vee)+{vlo}, V(mid)-1m)
Dhi n1 hi DCLAMP
Dlo lo n1 DCLAMP
Bout o1 0 V = V(n1)
Rout o1 out {rout}
Rq vcc vee {rq}
.model DCLAMP D(Is=1e-14 N=0.1)
.ends OPAMP_MACRO
* PA94-like high-voltage power operational amplifier (up to 900 V between its supplies), as the
* driver of a linear output stage
.subckt PA94 inp inn vcc vee out
X1 inp inn vcc vee out OPAMP_MACRO gbw=1Meg aol=200k vhi=3 vlo=3 slew=50Meg rq=680k
.ends PA94
* generic operational amplifier
.subckt OPAMP inp inn vcc vee out
X1 inp inn vcc vee out OPAMP_MACRO gbw=1Meg aol=200k vhi=0.1 vlo=0.1 slew=1Meg
.ends OPAMP
